<!-- this exercise was written by Chrissy Safranski as part of the PROTEUS grant-->

<setup>
  <module name="structures">
    <choiceInput inline>
      <shortDescription>various types of algebraic structures</shortDescription>
      <choice>a sum of two products</choice>
      <choice>a product of two sums</choice>
      <choice>a quotient of two products</choice>
      <choice>a quotient of two sums</choice>
      <choice>a sum of two quotients</choice>
      <choice>a quotient of a sum and a difference</choice>
      <choice>a difference of a quotient and a product</choice>
      <choice>a sum of a quotient and a product.</choice><choice>none of the listed structures</choice>
    </choiceInput>
    
  </module>
</setup>
<p>
      Each of the functions below could be described as having a specific algebraic structure.  Choose the correct structure (or that its structure is not listed) for each function.
  </p>

  <ol marker="a.">
    <li>
      <p><m>g(x) = \big(\sin(x) + \cos(x)\big) \cdot \big(e^x + \sqrt{x}\big)</m> is <module copy="$structures" name="c2"/></p>
    </li>
    <li>
      <p><m>f(x) = \sin(x) \cdot \cos(x) + e^x  \sqrt{x}</m> is <module copy="$structures" name="c1"/></p>
    </li>
    <li>
      <p><m>s(x) = \dfrac{\sin(x)}{e^x} + \dfrac{\cos(x)}{\sqrt{x}}</m> is <module copy="$structures" name="c5"/></p>
    </li>
    <li>
      <p><m>h(x) = \dfrac{\sin(x) \cdot \cos(x)}{e^x \sqrt{x}}</m> is <module copy="$structures" name="c3"/></p>
    </li>
    <li>
      <p><m>r(x) = \dfrac{\sin(x) + \cos(x)}{e^x + \sqrt{x}}</m> is <module copy="$structures" name="c4"/></p>
    </li>
  </ol>
  <answer>
    <award><when>$c1.selectedIndex=1 and $c2.selectedIndex=2 and $c3.selectedIndex=3 and $c4.selectedIndex=4 and $c5.selectedIndex=5</when></award>
  </answer>
